"notes":[
"Ranked online play (Multiplayer > Ranked): a matchmaking queue for Ranked 1v1 (solo, blind pick) and Ranked 4v4 Classic (with the pick / ban Draft; queue alone or with a party of 2-4). The relay matches players of similar rating (the search widens the longer you wait), shows how many are searching, and when it finds a match everyone gets 10 seconds to Accept (declining keeps you out of the queue for 2 minutes). The room opens and fills by itself.",
"Visible ranks from Bronze to Champion (Bronze to Diamond have divisions III, II, I). Your first 5 games are placements with bigger swings. The rating lives on the relay, never on your PC; every player's game reports the result and the majority counts. Leaving a ranked match early counts as a loss for you only.",
"Seasons of 8 weeks. Play 10 ranked games in a season for its skin (Season 1: Laurel, for every hero); your peak rank becomes a title (\"S1 Gold\"). At the end ratings move halfway back to 1000 and placements start again.",
"The Ranked screen has the season leaderboard (top 100, your friends highlighted, your position); the Profile has a Ranked tab (rank, peak, season record, your last 20 rating changes); ranks show on lobby slots and in the friends list. In 4v4, after 3 minutes without a match you can fill the seats with bots (unranked).",
"Needs the 0.45 relay: on an older one the Ranked card says so and everything else works as before.",
"The Codex (main menu, hero select) has four tabs now: Heroes, Modes, Maps and Rules, and a search box that finds anything by name (a hero, an ability, a twist, a map). Every mode has a page with its numbers first (Mayhem's multipliers, Draft's ban and pick order, every Weekly twist and its rule), every map has its minimap and what's special about it (Lantern Cross's shared causeway and two bridges), and the Rules tab explains income and interest, sends, the crystal, camps, bosses, duels, votes, Attack vs Ability Power, item actives, achievements and cosmetics, pings, spectating and the F9 overlay. Every hero page adds how to play the hero, how to play against them and the hero's Classic balance; fifteen heroes got the lore they were missing.",
"The first time you choose Draft, Mayhem, the Weekly Challenge, Survival, All-Random, 1v1, 2v2 or the Lantern Cross map, a small card explains how it works (Got it / Don't show tips; Enter or Esc close it). It never gets in the way of starting. The \"?\" on every Single Player card opens it again (or the mode's Codex page). Settings > Display > Mode tips turns the cards off; \"Show again\" resets them.",
"Tips while the line-up is revealed on hero select, during the setup minute and while you wait to revive, picked for your mode, map and hero (Mayhem tips in Mayhem, Malric tips when you play Malric).",
"Hover help: the Weekly card and the round line in a Weekly match give the twist's rule; the Draft board's step line says what the step means; the map buttons say what each map does differently."
]
}